# EXAMPLE ONLY - NEVER USE IN PRODUCTION. This key is public in the Postwerk
# repository, so anyone can test guessed addresses against hashes made with it.
#
# Hash key file (POSTWERK_HASH_KEY_FILE): keyed hashes of addresses after
# POSTWERK_PSEUDONYMIZE_AFTER. One key per line, <key-id>:<base64 of 32 bytes>;
# the first key line is the active key, later lines are old keys kept for
# lookups. Create your own with
#   docker run --rm postwerk:dev gen-key
# and use a different key than in the store key file.
